The '''Kuluba Accords''' ({{lang-bl|Akords de Kuluba}}; {{Langx|ca|Els Acords de Kuluba}}), officially known as the '''Peace and Reconciliation Accords''' ({{lang-bl|Akords de País y Reconciliación}}; {{Langx|ca|Els Acords de Pau i Reconciliació}}) comprise the agreements signed on 30 March 1982 in [[Kuluba]], [[Asikyira]], by the government's of [[Potocsí]] and [[Balisca]]. The Accords re-established diplomatic relations between the two countries which had been severed since the 1976 Potocsino agression against Balisca in the [[Camboriú War]], and formalized the idea of a cooperative exchange between the two countries, as well as the establishment of a demilitarized zone in the [[Marañón basin]].

==Content==

The Kuluba Accords consisted of 93 pages of detailed agreements and arrangements. In essence these covered withdrawal of forces, prisoner releases, the establishing of [[W:Condominium (international relations)|joint sovereignty]] and guarantees of [[Malvinas Islands#Baliscan visa policy|protection, non-discrimination and property rights for all residents]]. A section dealing with military issues provided for the permanent demilitarization of the Marañón basin.

